---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
	title="nth Term of an AP | Arithmetic Progressions | Class 10 Mathematics | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Learn the nth term formula aₙ = a + (n - 1)d for an Arithmetic Progression with step-by-step NCERT solved examples for Class 10."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/arithmetic-progressions" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Arithmetic Progressions</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">02</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 02 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS (NCERT)</div>
					<h1>nth Term of an <span>AP</span></h1>
					<p>
						Master the general term formula aₙ = a + (n - 1)d to find any term of an AP or calculate the number of terms.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · THE FORMULA -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · THE FORMULA</div>
					<h2>Formula for the nth Term</h2>
					<p>
						Let <em>a</em> be the first term and <em>d</em> be the common difference of an AP. The <strong>n-th term (aₙ)</strong> is given by:
					</p>

					<div class="formula-box">
						<strong>aₙ = a + (n - 1)d</strong>
						<span>where <em>a</em> = first term, <em>d</em> = common difference, <em>n</em> = term number, <em>aₙ</em> = n-th term (or last term <em>L</em>).</span>
					</div>

					<div class="idea-box">
						<div class="idea-icon">💡</div>
						<div class="idea-content">
							<strong>nth Term from the End</strong>
							<p>
								If an AP has <em>m</em> terms, the <em>n-th term from the end</em> is equal to the <strong>(m - n + 1)th term from the beginning</strong>, or:
								<br/>
								<strong>aₙ(end) = L - (n - 1)d</strong> &nbsp;(where <em>L</em> is the last term).
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLES -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLES</div>
					<h2>Step-by-Step Problem Solving</h2>

					<!-- Example 1 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1</span>
							<h3>Find the 10th term of the AP: 2, 7, 12...</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p>Given: a = 2, d = 7 - 2 = 5, n = 10.</p>
							<p>Using <em>aₙ = a + (n - 1)d</em>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								a₁₀ = 2 + (10 - 1) × 5<br/>
								a₁₀ = 2 + 9 × 5 = 2 + 45 = <strong>47</strong>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Example 2 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 2</span>
							<h3>Which term of the AP: 21, 18, 15... is -81?</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p>Given: a = 21, d = 18 - 21 = -3, aₙ = -81.</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								aₙ = a + (n - 1)d<br/>
								-81 = 21 + (n - 1)(-3)<br/>
								-81 - 21 = -3(n - 1)<br/>
								-102 = -3(n - 1) ⟹ n - 1 = 34 ⟹ <strong>n = 35</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:10px;">Hence, the <strong>35th term</strong> of the AP is -81.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>General term formula: <strong>aₙ = a + (n - 1)d</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>If <strong>aₙ</strong> is given, solve for <em>n</em> to find the position of a term.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p>Term number <em>n</em> must always be a <strong>positive integer</strong> (1, 2, 3...).</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/arithmetic-progressions/introduction" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>PREVIOUS LESSON</small>
								<strong>Introduction to AP</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/arithmetic-progressions/sum-of-n-terms" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>Sum of First n Terms</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- SIDEBAR -->
				<aside class="lesson-sidebar">
					<div class="sidebar-card">
						<div class="sidebar-title">ARITHMETIC PROGRESSIONS</div>
						<div class="progress-text">Lesson 02 of 04</div>
						<div class="progress-bar">
							<div style="width: 50%;"></div>
						</div>

						<div class="sidebar-lessons">
							<a href="/arithmetic-progressions/introduction" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>01</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Introduction to AP</strong>
									<small>First term (a) & difference (d)</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/arithmetic-progressions/nth-term" class="sidebar-lesson active">
								<span>02</span>
								<div>
									<strong>nth Term of an AP</strong>
									<small>Formula aₙ = a + (n-1)d</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/arithmetic-progressions/sum-of-n-terms" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>03</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Sum of First n Terms</strong>
									<small>Formula Sₙ = n/2[2a+(n-1)d]</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/arithmetic-progressions/pyqs" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>04</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Previous Year PYQs</strong>
									<small>CBSE 2020-2024 practice set</small>
								</div>
							</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</section>
		</div>
